From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:17:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pan/kmod: keep a reserve of system memory free from GPU
 allocations

The kernel's OOM handling can't get GPU memory back in time: kbase only
returns a process's GPU pages when its GPU context is torn down at exit.
When a process allocates GPU memory until the system runs out, killing
it frees nothing quickly, and the OOM killer works through the rest of
the system until the kernel panics. A game reached ~9 GB of GPU memory
on an 8 GB device this way; files written shortly before the panic were
lost.

Keep a reserve of system memory free instead, so an out-of-memory
situation ends in this process rather than in the system:

 - an allocation that would take MemAvailable below the reserve fails
   (VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY for the app);
 - if MemAvailable is below half the reserve anyway (memory growing
   outside our allocations, or an app retrying regardless) while this
   process holds more than that in GPU buffers, the process logs what
   it holds and kills itself, which frees its GPU memory on exit.

The reserve is RAM / 8 clamped to [768 MiB, 2 GiB], or
PAN_MEM_RESERVE_MB (0 disables the guard). MemAvailable is read once per
64 MiB of new allocations, and on every allocation once below the
reserve. Imported buffers aren't counted.

The memory budget reported through VK_EXT_memory_budget becomes what is
available above the reserve, so apps that follow it stay clear of the
refusals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: stop a runaway GPU allocator from exhausting system memory (kbase frees GPU pages only at context teardown, so the kernel OOM killer cannot recover it and the kernel panics); allocations that would cross a RAM-scaled reserve fail, and a process still allocating below half the reserve logs and kills itself
Upstream-commit: none (generic pan_kmod; upstream candidate)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11, 8 GB)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: csf-v11/085
Validation test: memhog (scratchpad Vulkan allocator): guard on refuses at MemAvailable 1005-1037 MiB (reserve 977 MiB), retries keep being refused; a second unguarded process driving MemAvailable to 485 MiB makes the guarded one log and SIGKILL itself, 5.4 GB returned, device unaffected; guard off reaches 394 MiB with no lmkd kills or memory pressure; racetest all cases 0/100 stale, controls 100/100; drawbench image checksums identical to csf-v11/192 (8 tests)
